The levels always fit within the same amount of space or so, like
80x16ish  (I think). So you should use the (s)earch command around
walls where you think there are likely to be more rooms until you find
a door, which you can (o)pen, or, if locked, (k)ick open.

The type of situation you describe is a bit uncommon but to that
uncommon, most levels are explorable minimal searching. I'm sure
frustrating for a new player. Don't let it get you down, once you get
the hang of a few of the basic nuances like that one the game gets
much more interesting.

As far as the jackals go, if you had run into a hallway so they could
only fight you one at a time you would have won. There are many other
strategies but that is a pretty un-spoily one, to try to use the
terrain, corners, hallways to your advantage.

Good luck!

